  "id": "anti-rotation-press",
  "name": "Anti-Rotation Press",
  "definition": "A narrow standing cable anti-rotation press with a hip-width parallel stance. The trunk resists rotation while the arms press and retract; this differs from the feet-together isometric band hold. Shoulder flexion, elbow extension and scapular protraction describe the press, not spinal rotation. Obliques are primary through the existing direction-aggregated opposition capability. Arm movers and the static lower-body and grip chain receive bounded anatomy-and-mechanics roles; the technical standard does not measure recruitment. Both cable sides are prescribed. Kneeling, band, overhead, stepping, twisting and timed-only holds remain excluded.",
